    "Waypoints": "Waypointy (WP)",
    "What this does. 1. gets the current gps coords from a nmea gps. 2. sends a guided mode WP to the AP at the hz you request. (remember this is limited to the gps you are using) How to use it 1. connect to ap. 2. take off, test guided mode is working. 3. open this and pick your comport, and baud rate for your nmea gps. 4. it should now be following you. NOTE: you must put the ap into guided mode manually": "What this does. 1. gets the current gps coords from a nmea gps. 2. sends a guided mode WP to the AP every 2 seconds. How to use it 1. connect to ap. 2. take off, test guided mode is working. 3. open this and pick your comport, and baud rate for your nmea gps. 4. it should now be following you.",
